From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:11:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] style(guide): typography for comfortable reading

Mulish is self-hosted at 300-600 only, yet the documents asked for 700
and 800, so every heading and bold word was synthesised. All weights are
600 now. Body text 16.5px / 1.7 on desktop (16 / 1.68 on phones) at a
68-character measure with text-wrap: pretty; one spacing rhythm
(paragraphs and lists end on 1em, headings take more space above than
below); a calmer heading scale (42 / 26 / 19.5); links underlined with
an offset; list markers in the brand orange; tables at 14.5px with more
padding and a tinted header; one h2 treatment for every document. The
generated documents (research, playbook v1-v3, admin v2-v3) follow:
same weights, small text one step up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Je1v64McNyB6XEu6gFgM4C
